# Common utils

## Purpose

Shared operator tooling belongs in `common/utils/` when introduced.

## Rules

- Utilities are **shared**, not tenant-specific business logic.
- Pass tenant/domain/capability context via **CLI args or config**, not hardcoded customer rules.
- Document behavior; avoid hidden side effects.

If `common/utils/` does not exist yet, do not invent tenant coupling in `scripts/`—prefer parameterized CLIs and follow ADR-0004 in `knowledge/decisions/`.
